invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_ifma.c
catches: rsa_ifma_model_test
reason: rsa_ifma_public starts the power from the base's words rather than
  digit_r2, so the first product writes base^2 / R' in place of base *
  R', and the result is off by a power of 2^(52n). This is the model of
  the prototype's mutant that converted an operand at the wrong bit
  offset: both leave a factor of a power of two outside the product's
  domain. bin/rsa_ifma_model_test compares rsa_vp1_cpu under the bit
  with rsa_vp1 and rsa_ifma_public with rsa_mont64_public.

--- old
    words_to_digits(power, digit_r2, k, modulus.digit_count, lane_count);
--- new
    (void)digit_r2;
    words_to_digits(power, words, k, modulus.digit_count, lane_count);
